DTLS post-quantum requirement is clearable (P15), so a server-flag rollback
takes effect without restarting the app.

Until now the requirement was one-way: qaudion::SetRequireDtlsPqc() (P8) did
`g_require_pqc.exchange(true)` and nothing could lower it, so an app that
turned it on from a server flag and later had that flag rolled back had to be
restarted before DTLS handshakes without X25519MLKEM768 worked again.

- rtc_base/qaudion_tuning.{h,cc}: `void SetRequireDtlsPqc(bool required = true)`.
  It stores the value and bumps TuningGeneration() only when the stored value
  changes, like the other reversible setters. The no-argument call still means
  "true" (the engine's runtime.cpp and any old caller compile unchanged).
  RequireDtlsPqc() is unchanged. The value is read once per DTLS handshake,
  when that handshake completes (P7's QaudionHandshakeMeetsPolicy()): a change
  applies to handshakes that complete after it and never touches a connection
  that is already established. The default stays false; strict builds already
  pin the transport level, not this knob.
- rtc_base/openssl_stream_adapter.cc (P7's QaudionHandshakeMeetsPolicy()):
  one `const bool require_pqc = qaudion::RequireDtlsPqc();` read feeds both the
  verdict and the `Q-AUDION dtls ... pqc_req=` line, so with a concurrent
  clear/set the log line always agrees with the decision that was taken
  (before, the function read the atomic twice).
- Android: `PeerConnectionFactory.setQaudionRequireDtlsPqc(boolean required)`;
  the no-argument overload stays for one release and calls it with true. The
  native method is now `nativeSetQaudionRequireDtlsPqcValue(boolean)` (JNI
  `jboolean`); the old argument-less native is gone. The new native name is
  deliberate: it makes the binary distinguishable from a P8-only build, so the
  G8 gate can pin it (an overload keeps the Java method name, and the JNI
  export of an argument-less/boolean pair would not differ).
- iOS: `+[RTCPeerConnectionFactory setQaudionRequireDtlsPqc:(BOOL)required]`;
  the old argument-less selector stays as an alias for YES for one release.
- Windows/engine: the C++ symbol changes to take a bool
  (...SetRequireDtlsPqc@qaudion@webrtc@@YAX_N@Z); engine/src/runtime.cpp calls
  the no-argument form and is unaffected.

Order: after P13/P14 (last of the audio/API series; m150/series). It edits
only text that P7, P8 and P13 added (qaudion_tuning.{h,cc} and the factory glue
of P8, the policy function of P7) and touches no file of any other patch in a
way that overlaps. No new GN target, no new dependency.

Touches (dir "."): rtc_base/qaudion_tuning.h, rtc_base/qaudion_tuning.cc,
rtc_base/openssl_stream_adapter.cc,
sdk/android/api/org/webrtc/PeerConnectionFactory.java,
sdk/android/src/jni/pc/peer_connection_factory.cc,
sdk/objc/api/peerconnection/RTCPeerConnectionFactory.h,
sdk/objc/api/peerconnection/RTCPeerConnectionFactory.mm.

Tests (not part of the series, added by m150/ci/apply-tests.py): T6 gets tests
for set true / read true, set false / read false and one TuningGeneration()
bump per real change; T11d (m150/tests/ssl_stream_adapter_strict_tests.inc,
spliced into ssl_stream_adapter_unittest.cc, strict config) handshakes a client
limited to X25519 against a strict server: refused while the requirement is on,
accepted once it is cleared.

